** More competitive decisions (P12 batch 6)

The notrump opener reopens with a double when their two-level overcall is
passed round to him and he is short in their suit (a common agreement: the
responder may have passed with a penalty double of his own).

1N-(2X)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:1} 0--2X, 15--17 hcp
  #STOP
#STOP

Opener after responder's preemptive raise over an overcall (5--9): game in the
major with 16+, 3NT with a stopper and 17+ after a minor.

1H-(1S)-3H-(P)-
4H = {prio:1} 16+ hcp
  #STOP
#STOP

1m-(1Y)-3m-(P)-
3N = {prio:1} 17+ hcp, stopper
  #STOP
#STOP

After our single raise and their competing bid, passed back to responder, a
responder with a fourth trump competes to the three level.

1M-(P)-2M-(2X)-P-(P)-
3M = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 4+M
  #STOP
#STOP

1M-(P)-2M-(3m)-P-(P)-
3M = {prio:1} 6--9 hcp, 4+M
  #STOP
#STOP

When their overcall of our one-level response is passed back, responder
reopens with notrump (8--10 and a stopper) or rebids a six-card suit.

1X-(P)-1Y-(1Z)-P-(P)-
1N = {prio:1} 8--10 hcp, stopper
  #STOP
2Y = {prio:2} 6--10 hcp, 6+Y
  #STOP
#STOP

After our sandwich-seat overcall is passed out at their raise, the overcaller
competes with a double (12+, short in their suit) or rebids a six-card suit.

(1X)-P-(1Y)-1Z-(2X)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:1} 12+ hcp, 0--2X
  #STOP
2Z = {prio:2} 11--16 hcp, 6+Z
  #STOP
#STOP

(1X)-P-(1Y)-1Z-(2Y)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:1} 12+ hcp, 0--2Y
  #STOP
2Z = {prio:2} 11--16 hcp, 6+Z
  #STOP
#STOP
